1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
This coin flip makes a million look easy. It's fucking not.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,020
Take a thousand dollars cash, or flip a coin.

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:11,500
Heads, your money doubles. But tails, you lose every damn cent.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,880
And no bailing early. You need ten heads in a row.

5
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,620
Do it, and you walk out with one million twenty-four thousand dollars.

6
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,700
Double-tap if you'd flip that coin without even thinking.

7
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:26,140
Three heads gets you eight thousand. Only one person in eight gets there.

8
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:30,800
Five heads is thirty-two thousand dollars, which is a real car, paid in full.

9
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:35,460
But now it's one in thirty-two. Everyone else is crying in the parking lot.

10
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:38,780
Send this to the friend who'd bet their whole rent on one flip.

11
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:42,480
Here's the brutal part. Line up one thousand twenty-four people.

12
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,020
Every flip, half of them get wiped out.

13
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:49,760
After ten flips, one person is left. Your odds? About a tenth of one percent.

14
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,660
That's like guessing the right day out of almost three years.

15
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,800
Follow, 'cause the ending flips this whole thing.

16
00:00:57,380 --> 00:01:01,580
The winner takes the million. The other thousand twenty-three get absolutely nothing.

17
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,820
Spread that million across the room, and it's a thousand bucks each.

18
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:08,280
Same as the boring cash. The coin just hides the losers.

19
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:11,060
So, cash or coin? One word.

